{
  "html": "<div id=\"BUV\" class=\"uplift front\">\n    <section id=\"course-front-body\" class=\"responsive-padding\" style=\"color: #2d3b45; background: none; padding-bottom: 0px; padding-top: 0px;\">\n        <article id=\"course-lesson-intro-text\" style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">\n            <h3 class=\"heavy\" style=\"margin: 0px; font-size: 2.7em; text-align: left;\">Welcome to Designing in Context (A): Territories, Clients and Audiences</h3>\n            <p style=\"text-align: left;\">In this module, students will understand the intersection of narrative, language, and user experience. Exploring \u2018context\u2019 further will introduce the nuances of audience needs and the importance of communication environments. The central theme is context-driven communication design, highlighting the need to adapt creative choices to the client and making meaningful connections between visual language, copy, narrative, and the final conveyed message.</p>\n        </article>\n        <div class=\"grid-row\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n            <article class=\"col-lg-4 buv-responsive-video-100\" style=\"padding-left: 12px; margin-bottom: 20px; margin-top: 20px;\">\n                <h3 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong><iframe title=\"Welcome to Designing in Context A\" src=\"https://buv.instructure.com/courses/7303/external_tools/retrieve?display=borderless&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fbuv.instructuremedia.com%2Flti%2Flaunch%3Fcustom_arc_launch_type%3Dlearn_embed%26custom_arc_media_id%3Dbe7f1bd6-d8b1-4019-89aa-dc978ce6f6a0-34880%26custom_arc_start_at%3D0\" width=\"850\" height=\"352\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\" webkitallowfullscreen=\"webkitallowfullscreen\" mozallowfullscreen=\"mozallowfullscreen\" allow=\"geolocation *; microphone *; camera *; midi *; encrypted-media *; autoplay *; clipboard-write *; display-capture *; fullscreen *\" data-studio-resizable=\"true\" data-studio-tray-enabled=\"true\" data-studio-convertible-to-link=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\"></iframe></strong></h3>\n            </article>\n            <article class=\"col-lg-8\" style=\"margin-top: 20px; padding-left: 12px;\">\n                <h3><strong>Learning Objectives for this module:</strong></h3>\n                <p><span style=\"color: #ba372a; font-size: 14pt;\">+ &nbsp;</span>Research and understand narrative, language, and user experience in communication design.</p>\n                <p><span style=\"color: #ba372a; font-size: 14pt;\">+ &nbsp;</span>Evidence pitching skills to effectively present design concepts.</p>\n                <p><span style=\"color: #ba372a; font-size: 14pt;\">+ &nbsp;</span>Proficiently communicate a message and meaning.</p>\n                <p><span style=\"color: #ba372a; font-size: 14pt;\">+ &nbsp;</span>Apply strategic frameworks to real-world scenarios to develop practical solutions.</p>\n                <div id=\"BUV\" class=\"uplift front\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n                    <section id=\"course-front-body\" class=\"responsive-padding\" style=\"color: #2d3b45; background: none; padding-bottom: 0px; padding-top: 0px;\"></section>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n        </div>\n    </section>\n</div>"
